{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/lavidalaguna/items/4351/", "pk": 4351, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/lavidalaguna/", "pk": 2623, "shortname": "lavidalaguna", "name": "La Vida Laguna", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Electric Bike Ride - Back Roads Laguna Tour", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 9, "unicode": "Electric Bike Ride - Back Roads Laguna Tour", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": true, "sold_out_text": "Full - Please call to book", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 12.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 12.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 2, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": true, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": false, "sortable_index": 500, "description": "#Electric Bike Ride - Back Roads Laguna Tour\n\n##Duration\n\n2 hours\n\n##About\nExperience the sublime beauty of Laguna Beach on this easy and historic loop that bypasses the busy streets. Pedal through the quaint Craftsman neighborhoods and gardens, access amazing view corridors, stop at Heisler Park to see the magnificent public art and experience the charming downtown commercial district with many artist residences.\n\nWe start our ride at our office in Central Laguna and head east, looping through Bluebird Canyon to experience the rolling inland hills. We will climb easily high above the city in the Mystic Hills neighborhood with a commanding view of our downtown district, Main Beach, and historic Laguna Hotel. Then we roll through our quaint downtown area, navigating picturesque neighborhoods past the historic Pyne Castle, with elevated ocean views in the bucolic and historic North Laguna. Then we head seaward to beautiful Crescent Bay Beach Park, with the best panoramic view of the coastline that extends from Dana Point all the way up to Palos Verdes in LA County! Following PCH, the tour takes us south through Heisler Park to view some of the town's amazing public art. Last, we'll cycle back through the downtown village and the Central Laguna neighborhood, home to early California Craftsman bungalows. \n\n **Details**\n\n- **Time**: Custom tours daily\n- **Level**: Easy ride with electric assist, however, we do share the road with cars \n- **Location**: 1121 Glenneyre St,  Laguna Beach\n- **Inclusions**: Electric pedal assist 7-speed fat-tire bikes, helmet, water\n- **What to bring**: shorts, tennis shoes, sunblock, sunglasses\n- **Ages**: Anyone at least 5' tall and 15 years or older can ride\n\n**Directions, parking, and what to bring are contained in the reservation confirmation email.**", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "With our trailer, chase vehicle and fleet of more than 40 speed mountain bikes, we have developed a special aptitude for leading group bike rides throughout Southern California. No matter what your groups desires, we have a ride.\n\nLaguna Back Roads: Experience the sublime beauty of Laguna Beach on this safe and historic loop that bypasses Pacific Coast Highway. Pedal the quaint Craftsman neighborhoods and gardens, access amazing view corridors, stop at Heisler Park to see the magnificent public art, experience the charming downtown commercial district, and many artists residences.", "location": "Laguna Beach, CA", "booking_notes": "Thank you for choosing **La Vida Laguna** for your coastal bike adventure!\n\n**PLEASE NOTE:** We share the same address with our neighbors to the left of our entrance.   Our shop has the prominent white door and frame. You will see a La Vida Laguna sign in the window. \n\n[![Description of image](https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/wEveEAZoRkiwjgCgxYw7)!](https://goo.gl/maps/9UCxAw4dm9DDDgfq9)\n\t\n**Parking:** There are four parking spots along Oak Street for our office that remain first come first serve. If you are unable to park in one of the spots, there is plenty of metered parking along Glenneyre (they take credit cards), or free parking in the adjacent neighborhoods.\n\n**Suggested Attire:** shorts, leggings, tennis shoes, sunglasses, and sunblock. No purses or hanging bags. \n\n**We provide:** pedal assist ebike, water, and helmet\n\nMust be 4'8\"' or taller\n\nThis is an easy ebike ride with intermediate terrain, approx. 10 mile ride with moderate climbs and descents. Not strenuous with pedal assist bikes!\n\nIf you have any questions, please do not hesitate to call (949) 275-7544!\n\nWe look forward to biking with you!", "cancellation_notes": "Because we have limited capacities, this booking is not cancelable within 48 hours.  Cancellations received 48 hours prior to tour will receive a full refund. If La Vida Laguna cancels the tour because of unsafe conditions, you will receive a full refund.  Due to potential changes in weather conditions, we reserve the right to cancel a tour at any time.", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "2 hours • See all of Laguna Beach from local's perspective through back roads • Ages 15+", "short_description": "2 hours • See all of Laguna Beach from local's perspective through back roads • Ages 15+", "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/lavidalaguna/items/4351/images/521903/", "pk": 521903, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/UrwqlOveRG21COCHeNuc", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/UrwqlOveRG21COCHeNuc", "compan